    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d599">

                <pb facs="0742" n="618" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg618"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/1285</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Japanese Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Shidehara</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-09-16"><hi rendition="#italic">September 16,
                        1921</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I am now in receipt of a
                    telegram from Tokio informing me that the outline of the terms of settlement on
                    the Shantung question, which Japan proposed to China on September 7, and which I
                    had the pleasure of communicating to you, has just been published in a <hi
                        rendition="#italic">communiqué</hi> of the Foreign Office at Tokio. The <hi
                        rendition="#italic">communiqué</hi> is prefaced by an explanatory statement,
                    copy of which I venture to enclose herewith for your information.</p>
                <p>Believe me [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">K. Shidehara</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d599-a1.xml" xpointer="d599-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
